---
import LessonLayout from '../../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';
---
<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; The Dignity of the Human Person" cic="CCC 1700-1715" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
  <li>What does the book of Genesis say about the creation of the human being?</li>
  <li>What does the dignity of the human person consist of, according to the Catechism?</li>
  <li>What consequences did original sin have on human dignity?</li>
  <li>What does it mean that the human being is a &laquo;person&raquo;?</li>
  <li>According to St. Leo the Great, what should Christians recognize?</li>
</ol>
</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. What really makes you feel valuable? Where does your sense of self-worth come from?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Think about the voices you hear when you evaluate yourself. Who are they? What do they tell you?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Is there someone you find it difficult to treat with dignity? Why?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">It could be someone who has hurt you, someone you despise, or someone simply different from you.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. In what area of your life do you find it hard to live according to your dignity as a child of God?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Your thoughts, words, actions, relationships, use of time&hellip;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. What would change in your life if you truly believed you were &laquo;the image of God&raquo;?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Try to be concrete: a decision, a conversation, a change of habit.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. How can you recognize and honor the dignity of the people around you this week?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">In your family, your work, your school, your community.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. The mirror of dignity</h4>
<p>Stand in front of a mirror and look into your eyes. Say aloud: &laquo;You are the image of God. God loves you. You have infinite dignity.&raquo; Do this every day this week and write how you feel.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. The portrait of dignity</h4>
<p>Choose a person you find difficult to treat with respect (a difficult coworker, a conflicting family member, someone with a different opinion). Write three things that God sees in them that you do not see.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. A concrete action</h4>
<p>Do one thing this week that honors your dignity as a child of God: take care of your body, dedicate time to prayer, say no to something that degrades you, help someone in need.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>&laquo;God created man in his own image; in the image of God he created him; male and female he created them.&raquo;</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; Genesis 1:27</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Lord, you who created me in your image,<br />
help me to know myself as you see me.<br />
Heal the wounds that darken your image in me,<br />
and teach me to see your face in every person I meet.<br />
May I always live according to my dignity as your child,<br />
and never forget that I was created for love and beatitude.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>
</section>

<section class="content">

<hr />

<div class="downloads">
<a href="javascript:window.print()" class="download-btn">Print Workbook</a>
</div>
</section>

</LessonLayout>
